NeuralAquarium
A living digital aquarium powered by physics simulation, neural networks, and genetic algorithms — all built from scratch, no ML libraries.

What is this? Emergent Aquarium is an interactive ecosystem simulation disguised as a fish tank. Each fish is an autonomous organism with energy, age, and DNA — driven by real algorithms running under the hood:

Physics engine with repulsive forces and spring dynamics governing movement Neural network (built from scratch with backpropagation) that learns from the ecosystem's behavior in real-time Genetic algorithm with tournament selection, crossover, and mutation that evolves the population over generations Markov chains & Perlin noise generating organic, procedural behavior K-means clustering & dimensionality reduction analyzing the population structure

Fish are born, compete for energy, reproduce, and die. The fittest survive. The neural network observes and adapts. You control the environment.

Features Real-time ecosystem — fish live, breed, and die based on energy and environmental pressures Self-training neural network — a 4→12→8→4 network trains on ecosystem state every few ticks, learning to predict system health Genetic evolution — organisms inherit traits from parents with mutation; consume_rate evolves across generations Interactive controls — tune current strength, turbulence, schooling behavior, and hunger in real-time Immersive visuals — animated fish with fins, light rays, caustics, swaying plants, bubbles, and a sandy floor Live telemetry — population timeline, neural network error curve, generation tracking, and per-fish stats

Quick Start:

pip install -r requirements.txt python run.py Open http://localhost:5000 and do whatever

