The Science This project demonstrates emergence — complex, lifelike behavior arising from simple rules:

No fish is programmed to "swim" — movement emerges from repulsive forces, spring connections, and random noise No fish is told to "flock" — schooling behavior emerges from the cohesion parameter pulling organisms toward shared attractors No fish is designed to "evolve" — natural selection happens because organisms with lower consume_rate survive longer and reproduce more The neural network isn't pre-trained — it learns by observing the ecosystem, getting better at predicting system health as the simulation runs

The same principles drive real biological systems, from bacterial colonies to bird flocks.

Technical Details Zero external ML/AI dependencies. Every algorithm is implemented from scratch in pure Python:

Matrix multiplication, sigmoid activation, and backpropagation (gamma.py) Tournament selection, single-point crossover, and Gaussian mutation (delta.py) Markov chain construction and random walks (epsilon.py) 1D Perlin noise with octave layering (epsilon.py) K-means clustering with random initialization (epsilon.py) Random projection for dimensionality reduction (epsilon.py) N-body repulsion and Hooke's law spring simulation (alpha.py)

The only dependency is Flask for serving the web interface.

Requirements

Python 3.8+ Flask 3.0

That's it.

